# HeroUI Provider Setup (Next.js App Router)

To enable HeroUI context (theming, routing integration, etc.) throughout your application, you need to wrap your application's root layout with the `HeroUIProvider`.

1.  **Create a Client Component Provider Wrapper:**
    Create a file like `app/providers.tsx` and mark it as a client component (`'use client'`). Import `HeroUIProvider` from `@heroui/react` and wrap the `children`.

    ```tsx
    // app/providers.tsx
    'use client'

    import {HeroUIProvider} from '@heroui/react'
    // Optionally import and wrap other providers like NextThemesProvider
    import { ThemeProvider as NextThemesProvider } from "next-themes"
    
    export function Providers({children}: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
      // Add logic like handling mounted state if needed for theme providers
      return (
        <HeroUIProvider>
          {/* <NextThemesProvider attribute="class" defaultTheme="dark"> */}
            {children}
          {/* </NextThemesProvider> */}
        </HeroUIProvider>
      )
    }
    ```

2.  **Integrate into Root Layout:**
    Import the `Providers` component into your `app/layout.tsx` and use it to wrap the main content (`children`).

    ```tsx
    // app/layout.tsx
    import { Providers } from "./providers";
    
    export default function RootLayout({children}) {
      return (
        <html lang="en">
          <body>
            <Providers>
              {/* Your other layout components (Navbar, Sidebar, etc.) */}
              {children}
            </Providers>
          </body>
        </html>
      );
    }
    ```

*Based on documentation snippet: [Defining Client-Side HeroUI Provider (App Directory)](mdc:https:/github.com/heroui-inc/heroui/blob/canary/apps/docs/content/docs/frameworks/nextjs.mdx#_snippet_5)*
